How about:
4) Edit the high score list, and insert your name with one point more than
   his top score.  Be sure to use a Tourist class for your character.
   If he beats that score, repeat (This is really good if you're playing
   version 3.1.0, where tourists can't win.  Tell him that Tourists are
   a lot easier get high scores with, and hope he tries).

5) Recognize that you're REALLY, REALLY nasty, and wait until he gets a
   to a point where he's got the bell of opening.  Erase all his save 
   positions except for that one, and then start that one.  Hide his 
   Bell of opening under a boulder, then wish for a "Bell" (to get a 
   wish, use quaff at a fountain using the save restore trick until
   you are granted one).  Then take the bell and name it Bell of 
   Opening.

   This way, he'll continue to play for days/weeks/months, thinking
   he's finally going to win.  Unless he notices that the Bell of 
   Opening is actually "a bell called Bell of Opening", he won't even
   know you've been there.  Then sit back and chuckle as he can't get
   past the "vibrating square".

6) If he's got a save position where he's already got the Amulet of 
   Yendor, use the same technique as (4) to replace it with a cheap
   plastic imatation.  Hide the real one under a boulder on level 30.
   When he gets to the endgame, he'll realize something is wrong, and
   go back to a previous save position.  Eventually, you'll hear him
   pound his head on the desk in frustration, because he can't find the
   real one anywhere.

   If the sound of him pounding his head on the desk starts to bother you,
   then tell him that in one of your games you found the real Amulet
   under a boulder on level 30.  He'll laugh and say that was only in a 
   really early version of nethack, but get him to go back and check 
   somehow.  When he finds it there, he'll be astounded by your knowledge
   of nethack.

